      "name": "CopyDataToGlobalBuffer",
      "signature": "void CopyDataToGlobalBuffer(void * pSourceData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies a 288-byte data buffer from source memory to a global buffer and updates the global pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI and EDI registers on stack for preservation\n2. Load source pointer from ECX register (fastcall parameter)\n3. Initialize copy counter to 0x48 (72 double words = 288 bytes)\n4. Set destination pointer to global buffer address 0x6f87c558\n5. Execute REP MOVSD to copy 72 dwords from source to destination\n6. Restore EDI and ESI registers from stack\n7. Update global pointer at 0x6f87c550 to point to destination buffer\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceData (ECX): Pointer to source memory containing data to copy (288 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fixed copy size of 288 bytes (0x48 dwords)\n  - Destination buffer is always at 0x6f87c558\n  - Global pointer reference at 0x6f87c550 always updated to 0x6f87c558\n  - Uses fastcall convention with parameter in ECX register\n\nData Layout:\n  Global destination buffer: 0x6f87c558 (288 bytes)\n  Global pointer reference: 0x6f87c550 (4 bytes)",
