      "name": "AmsgExit",
      "signature": "void AmsgExit(int nExitCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exit the application with optional console message display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if console display is enabled by testing DAT_1003c8bc == 1\n2. If not enabled, check secondary condition: DAT_1003c8bc == 0 AND DAT_1003c8c0 == 1\n3. If either condition true, call FUN_1001f7e7() to display console message\n4. Call FUN_1001f820(nExitCode) to perform cleanup operations with provided exit code\n5. Call exit function through function pointer PTR___exit_1002e48c with code 0xff\n6. Function does not return (terminates process)\n\nParameters:\nnExitCode (int): Exit code to pass to cleanup function FUN_1001f820\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return (terminates process execution)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Always calls exit with hardcoded 0xff regardless of input exit code\n- Console message display depends on two global flag variables\n- Function pointer call suggests dynamic linking or runtime binding\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1 - Console display enabled flag value\n0x0 - Console display disabled flag value  \n0xff - Hardcoded exit code passed to exit function (255 decimal)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
