      "name": "ValidateAndInitializePointers",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndInitializePointers(uint * pOutputData1, uint * pOutputData2, uint * pOutputData3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates three pointer parameters and initializes output parameters with global data values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pOutputData1 is NULL, set error code 0x23b if invalid\n2. Check if pOutputData2 is NULL, set error code 0x23c if invalid\n3. Check if pOutputData3 is NULL, set error code 0x23d if invalid\n4. If all three pointers are valid, copy three global data values to output pointers\n5. On validation failure, call GetReturnAddress() to get return info, then CleanupAndAbort()\n6. Call _exit(-1) to terminate process on error\n\nParameters:\npOutputData1 [ECX]: First output pointer to receive global data from 0x6f87caa8\npOutputData2 [EDX]: Second output pointer to receive global data from 0x6f87ca90\npOutputData3 [ESP+4]: Third output pointer to receive global data from 0x6f87ca80\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value on success path)\nOn validation failure: triggers error handling and process termination\n\nSpecial Cases:\nError code 0x23b: pOutputData1 is NULL\nError code 0x23c: pOutputData2 is NULL\nError code 0x23d: pOutputData3 is NULL\nAll three pointers must be non-NULL for successful initialization",
