      "name": "InitializeGraphicsResources",
      "signature": "int InitializeGraphicsResources(int graphicsConfig, int resolutionMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes graphics rendering system by setting up palette, font, and screen resolution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store graphics configuration reference in global variable\n2. Call graphics initialization routine (FUN_6f876d00)\n3. Clear 256 dwords of graphics data buffer (DAT_6f87c680)\n4. Create LOGPALETTE structure with 256 zero-initialized palette entries\n5. Create standard font (Courier, size 10pt, weight 400)\n6. Store palette handle in DAT_6f87ca84 and font handle in DAT_6f87c040\n7. Initialize state counter (DAT_6f87ca98) to 0\n8. Set screen width in pixels based on resolution mode:\n   - resolutionMode 0: 640 pixels (0x280)\n   - resolutionMode 3: 1344 pixels (0x540)\n   - default: 800 pixels (0x320)\n9. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\nECX: graphicsConfig - Graphics configuration reference/pointer\nEDX: resolutionMode - Screen resolution mode (0=640, 3=1344, other=800)\n\nReturns:\nEAX: 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Palette always initialized with 256 zero black entries (no custom colors)\n- Font size fixed at 10pt with weight 400 (normal)\n- All palette entry fields (peRed, peGreen, peBlue, peFlags) set to zero",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
