      "name": "ValidateAndRenderCell",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndRenderCell(void * pObject, int selector)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates object placement constraints and renders object if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pObject parameter using validation function\n2. Read object dimensions/position from pObject+0x3c (likely structure offset)\n3. Query cell width and height constraints from global configuration\n4. Validate horizontal placement: x + width < max_width AND x + width > -1\n5. Validate vertical placement: y + height >= 0 AND y + height - cell_height < max_height\n6. If all bounds pass, retrieve selector-based configuration values\n7. Call render function with object pointer and configuration parameters\n8. Return 1 for success, 0 for validation/bounds failure\n\nParameters:\npObject: Pointer to game object structure being validated/rendered\nselector: Index/selector value determining configuration lookup (0-based index)\n\nReturns:\n1 if object successfully validated and rendered, 0 if validation or bounds check failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 immediately if pObject fails initial validation check\n- selector=0 skips certain configuration lookups\n- Special handling when selector value equals 7 (accesses alternate data table offset)\n\nStructure Layout:\nObject Structure Accessed:\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type        Description\n+0x3c   4     cell_or_pos_ref    dword       Reference to cell/position data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
