      "name": "ValidateCellBounds",
      "signature": "uint ValidateCellBounds(int baseOffset, uint * pSourceBounds, uint maxBound, uint * pOutputBounds)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and calculates cell-based coordinate bounds with constraints.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate horizontal bounds from source structure at [0] and [4]\\n2. Apply horizontal maximum constraint from global DAT_6f87ca80\\n3. Calculate cell width using D2CMP_GetCellWidth for the given bounds\\n4. Check if calculated width fits within maxBound parameter\\n5. Validate vertical bounds from source structure at [8] and [0xc]\\n6. Apply vertical maximum constraint from global DAT_6f87ca90\\n7. Calculate cell height using Ordinal_10069\\n8. Combine horizontal and vertical into 2D bounds\\n9. Calculate output dimensions based on overlap with limits\\n10. Validate final height value is positive; abort if not\\n\\nParameters:\\n- baseOffset (ECX): Base offset value for coordinate calculations (typically 0)\\n- pSourceBounds (EDX): Pointer to source bounds array [minH, maxH, minV, maxV]\\n- maxBound (Stack[4]): Maximum allowed boundary value for horizontal extent\\n- pOutputBounds (Stack[8]): Pointer to output bounds array [minH, maxH, minV, maxV]\\n\\nReturns:\\n- 0 on success: output bounds written to pOutputBounds\\n- 1 on validation failure: bounds do not meet constraints\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Uses global constraints DAT_6f87ca80 (horizontal max) and DAT_6f87ca90 (vertical max)\\n- Clamps maximum bounds to global limits before calculation\\n- Validates that calculated dimensions are positive; exits with code -1 if invalid\\n- Performs multiple boundary checks before writing output\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type    Description\\n0       4     minHorizontal   uint    Minimum horizontal bound\\n4       4     maxHorizontal   uint    Maximum horizontal bound\\n8       4     minVertical     uint    Minimum vertical bound\\n12      4     maxVertical     uint    Maximum vertical bound",
