      "name": "ValidateAndProcessTiles",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndProcessTiles(int pLevelData, uint maxY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and processes all tiles in a level within specified coordinate bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate level state via Ordinal_10106 call - returns 0 if invalid\n2. Load global bounds from DAT_6f87ca80 (width), DAT_6f87ca90 (height + 0x20)\n3. Calculate min X based on input maxY parameter (via Y-type encoding)\n4. Iterate through tile array at pLevelData+0x54 with 0x14-byte stride\n5. Extract X coordinate from word at tile+0x0, add to base X (ESI)\n6. Extract Y coordinate from word at tile+0x2, add to base Y (stack)\n7. Validate X in range [minX, width) and Y in range [-0x20, height)\n8. If valid: extract tile type via SAR by 0x5 bits, read flags from lookup table\n9. Call function pointer at DAT_6f87ca94+0x10 with coordinates and flags\n10. Return 1 if any tiles processed, 0 if none\n\nParameters:\n  pLevelData (ECX): Pointer to level/map structure with count at +0x50, array at +0x54\n  maxY (EDX): Maximum Y coordinate boundary value\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: 1 if at least one tile was processed and validated, 0 if none\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Level Data Structure (from pLevelData):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n  0x50    4     tileCount         dword     Number of tiles in array\n  0x54    4     tileArrayPtr      pointer   Points to tile array (0x14-byte strides)\n\n  Tile Entry Structure (0x14 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n  0x0     2     tileX             sword     X coordinate (relative to base)\n  0x2     2     tileY             sword     Y coordinate (relative to base)\n  0x10    2     tileType          sword     Tile type/flags",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
