      "comment": "Fills a rectangular region with a repeated byte value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that rect.right >= rect.left (else abort with error code 0x15e)\n2. Validate that rect.bottom >= rect.top (else abort with error code 0x15f)\n3. Clamp rectangle boundaries to valid range [0, maxWidth) x [0, maxHeight):\n   - If rect.left < 0, set to 0\n   - If rect.right > maxWidth, set to maxWidth - 1\n   - If rect.top < 0, set to 0\n   - If rect.bottom > maxHeight, set to maxHeight - 1\n4. Calculate actual fill dimensions:\n   - width = rect.right - rect.left\n   - height = rect.bottom - rect.top\n5. Skip filling if width or height is zero\n6. Calculate starting buffer address: (rect.top * maxWidth + rect.left) + baseBuffer\n7. Fill each row of the rectangle using optimized block operations:\n   - For each row, fill width dwords using STOSD (dword fill)\n   - Fill remaining width bytes using STOSB (byte fill)\n   - Move to next row by adding maxWidth stride\n\nParameters:\n- pRect: Pointer to rectangle structure with left, top, right, bottom boundaries\n- fillByte: Byte value to fill the region with (replicated to fill dwords)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Validates bounds before processing and aborts on invalid ranges\n- Clamps values to [0, maxWidth) x [0, maxHeight)\n- Uses optimized STOSD/STOSB for fast memory filling\n- Handles non-aligned region widths by filling bulk dwords then remaining bytes\n\nStructure Layout (rectangle parameter):\nOffset | Size | Field  | Type | Description\n-------|------|--------|------|------------------\n0x0    | 4    | left   | int  | Left edge X coordinate\n0x4    | 4    | top    | int  | Top edge Y coordinate\n0x8    | 4    | right  | int  | Right edge X coordinate\n0xc    | 4    | bottom | int  | Bottom edge Y coordinate\nTotal: 16 bytes",
