      "name": "ProcessPointRegion",
      "signature": "void ProcessPointRegion(int * pCoordinates, char distance, undefined1 param3)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates a bounding rectangle centered at given point and processes the region.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if distance parameter is non-zero (if zero, skip processing)\n2. Calculate expansion distance: distance - 1\n3. Extract X and Y coordinates from pCoordinates array\n4. Calculate rectangle boundaries:\n   - left = X - expandDistance\n   - top = Y - expandDistance\n   - right = X + 1 + expandDistance\n   - bottom = Y + 1 + expandDistance\n5. Initialize rectangle structure using SetRect API\n6. Process the defined region via FUN_6f877230\n\nParameters:\n- pCoordinates: Pointer to [X, Y] coordinate pair (2 ints)\n- distance: Distance/radius value (1-255), actual expansion = distance - 1\n- param3: Opaque parameter passed to region processor function\n\nReturns:\n- void (result passed via region processor callback)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Distance of 0 causes function to return without processing\n- Expansion distance calculated as (distance - 1) in range 0-254\n- Rectangle encompasses area from [X-exp, Y-exp] to [X+1+exp, Y+1+exp]\n- Region processing delegated to FUN_6f877230 callback\n\nStructure Layout (tagRECT):\nOffset | Size | Field      | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|------------------\n0x0    | 4    | left       | int  | Rectangle left edge\n0x4    | 4    | top        | int  | Rectangle top edge\n0x8    | 4    | right      | int  | Rectangle right edge\n0xc    | 4    | bottom     | int  | Rectangle bottom edge\nTotal: 16 bytes",
