      "name": "ValidateItemsInArea",
      "signature": "int ValidateItemsInArea(int pUnitInventory, int yCoordinate)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates items in a unit's inventory against coordinate bounds and invokes callbacks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10106 with unit pointer and parameters; exit if returns 0\n2. Load global boundary configuration from DAT_6f87ca90 and DAT_6f87ca80\n3. Determine coordinate bound limits based on boundMode value:\n   - Mode 0: maxXLimit = DAT_6f87ca80, minXBound = -0x20\n   - Mode 1: maxXLimit = DAT_6f87ca80 / 2, minXBound = -0x20\n   - Mode 2: maxXLimit = DAT_6f87ca80, minXBound = (DAT_6f87ca80 / 2) - 0x20\n4. Get item count from [pUnitInventory + 0x50]\n5. Loop through each item in array at [pUnitInventory + 0x54]:\n   - Each item is 0x14 bytes long\n   - Load X coordinate from item offset 0, Y coordinate from item offset 2\n   - Add parameter offsets: itemXCoord = itemX + xCoordinate, itemYCoord = itemY + yCoordinate\n   - Validate bounds: minXBound <= itemXCoord < maxXLimit AND -0x20 < itemYCoord < (maxYBound + 0x20)\n6. If item passes validation:\n   - Set foundItem flag to 1\n   - Load callback function pointer from [pUnitInventory + 0x54 + itemIndex + 0x10]\n   - Load callback dispatch table from DAT_6f87ca94\n   - If [DAT_6f87ca88 + 0x14] == 0: call [DAT_6f87ca94 + 4] with Y coordinate\n   - Otherwise: call [DAT_6f87ca94 + 0x14] with Y coordinate and 0xc0\n\nParameters:\n  pUnitInventory (ECX): Pointer to unit/player inventory structure\n    +0x50: Item count (dword)\n    +0x54: Pointer to item array (each item 0x14 bytes)\n  yCoordinate (EDX): Y-axis coordinate offset for validation\n  xCoordinate (implicit via ESI): X-axis coordinate offset for validation\n  boundMode (implicit via ESP+0x24): Boundary limit mode selector (0, 1, or 2)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: 1 if any item passed validation and callback was invoked, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic offsets: 0x50 (item count), 0x54 (item array), 0x10 (item ID in item structure)\n  Magic boundary value: -0x20 (lower Y boundary), 0x20 (max Y boundary offset)\n  Callback dispatch varies based on flag at DAT_6f87ca88 + 0x14\n  Item array stride: 0x14 bytes per item\n  Coordinate offsets: shorts at item[0] and item[2]",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
